    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-at-sea-act-2000-sch-2-sec-6a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "6A Criminal laws applicable in the Greater Sunrise special regime",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-at-sea-act-2000#sch-2-sec-6a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-at-sea-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-at-sea-act-2000.pdf, p.12",
      "values:originalText": "area\n\n(1) The provisions of the substantive criminal law of the Northern\nTerritory from time to time apply to a criminal act done in the\nGreater Sunrise special regime area that is connected with, or\narises out of, petroleum activities as if the act had been done in the\nNorthern Territory.\n\n(2) However, the relevant substantive criminal law does not apply to:\n\n(a) an act done on or from a ship or aircraft; or\n\n(b) an act done by a national of Timor-Leste who is not also a\nnational of Australia; or\n\n(c) an act done by a permanent resident of Timor-Leste who is\nnot also a national of Australia.\n\n(3) Proceedings for an offence against a substantive criminal law as\napplied under this section may not be instituted against a person if:\n\n(a) the person has been acquitted or discharged without penalty\nin proceedings for an offence against a law in force in\nTimor-Leste arising out of the same act; or\n\n(b) the person has incurred a penalty under a law in force in\nTimor-Leste for such an offence; or\n\n(c) a competent authority of Timor-Leste has decided not to\nprosecute the person for such an offence.\n\n(4) A prosecution for an offence against a law applied by\nsubsection (1) may only be heard and determined if the\nAttorney-General consents in writing to the prosecution.\n\n\nCooperation between Australia and Timor-Leste in the enforcement of criminal law",
      "skos:definition": "area\n\n(1) The provisions of the substantive criminal law of the Northern\nTerritory from time to time apply to a criminal act done in the\nGreater Sunrise special regime area that is connected with, or\narises out of, petroleum activities as if the act had been done in the\nNorthern Territory.\n\n(2) However, the relevant substantive criminal law does not apply to:\n\n(a) an act done on or from a ship or aircraft; or\n\n(b) an act done by a national of Timor-Leste who is not also a\nnational of Australia; or\n\n(c) an act done by a permanent resident of Timor-Leste who is\nnot also a national of Australia.\n\n(3) Proceedings for an offence against a substantive criminal law as\napplied under this section may not be instituted against a person if:\n\n(a) the person has been acquitted or discharged without penalty\nin proceedings for an offence against a law in force in\nTimor-Leste arising out of the same act; or\n\n(b) the person has incurred a penalty under a law in force in\nTimor-Leste for such an offence; or\n\n(c) a competent authority of Timor-Leste has decided not to\nprosecute the person for such an offence.\n\n(4) A prosecution for an offence against a law applied by\nsubsection (1) may only be heard and determined if the\nAttorney-General consents in writing to the prosecution.\n\n\nCooperation between Australia and Timor-Leste in the enforcement of criminal law",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-at-sea-act-2000-sch-2-sec-6a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-at-sea-act-2000-sch-2-sec-6a-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-at-sea-act-2000-sch-2-sec-6a-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-at-sea-act-2000-sch-2-sec-6a-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4a91ee5f0106c2b35c11c168352f0abfbf4fc86165c62d6fb51b5232dfc692e6"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-at-sea-act-2000#sch-2-sec-6a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "6A Criminal laws applicable in the Greater Sunrise special regime",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 12,
      "values:originalText": "area\n\n(1) The provisions of the substantive criminal law of the Northern\nTerritory from time to time apply to a criminal act done in the\nGreater Sunrise special regime area that is connected with, or\narises out of, petroleum activities as if the act had been done in the\nNorthern Territory.\n\n(2) However, the relevant substantive criminal law does not apply to:\n\n(a) an act done on or from a ship or aircraft; or\n\n(b) an act done by a national of Timor-Leste who is not also a\nnational of Australia; or\n\n(c) an act done by a permanent resident of Timor-Leste who is\nnot also a national of Australia.\n\n(3) Proceedings for an offence against a substantive criminal law as\napplied under this section may not be instituted against a person if:\n\n(a) the person has been acquitted or discharged without penalty\nin proceedings for an offence against a law in force in\nTimor-Leste arising out of the same act; or\n\n(b) the person has incurred a penalty under a law in force in\nTimor-Leste for such an offence; or\n\n(c) a competent authority of Timor-Leste has decided not to\nprosecute the person for such an offence.\n\n(4) A prosecution for an offence against a law applied by\nsubsection (1) may only be heard and determined if the\nAttorney-General consents in writing to the prosecution.\n\n\nCooperation between Australia and Timor-Leste in the enforcement of criminal law"
    },
