    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-at-sea-act-2000-sch-2-sec-6b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "6B Transit of persons accused of offences against the laws of",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-at-sea-act-2000#sch-2-sec-6b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-at-sea-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-at-sea-act-2000.pdf, p.13",
      "values:originalText": "Timor-Leste\n\n(1) If Timor-Leste wishes to transport in custody through Australia a\nperson (the accused) who has been arrested for an offence against\na criminal law in force in Timor-Leste that applies in the Greater\nSunrise special regime area, the following provisions apply:\n\n(a) the accused may be transported in custody through Australia;\nand",
      "skos:definition": "Timor-Leste\n\n(1) If Timor-Leste wishes to transport in custody through Australia a\nperson (the accused) who has been arrested for an offence against\na criminal law in force in Timor-Leste that applies in the Greater\nSunrise special regime area, the following provisions apply:\n\n(a) the accused may be transported in custody through Australia;\nand",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-at-sea-act-2000-sch-2-sec-6b-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-at-sea-act-2000-sch-2-sec-6b-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "62ea1d5261b62cf8e8ae7cd406035ba0a583ebdbb64ecca96571192b4123ec5f",
      "skos:note": "Permits transportation of accused persons through Australia"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-at-sea-act-2000#sch-2-sec-6b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "6B Transit of persons accused of offences against the laws of",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 13,
      "values:originalText": "Timor-Leste\n\n(1) If Timor-Leste wishes to transport in custody through Australia a\nperson (the accused) who has been arrested for an offence against\na criminal law in force in Timor-Leste that applies in the Greater\nSunrise special regime area, the following provisions apply:\n\n(a) the accused may be transported in custody through Australia;\nand"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-at-sea-act-2000-sch-2-sec-6b-norm",
