    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-at-sea-act-2000-sch-1-sec-6",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "6 Effect of the agreement",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-at-sea-act-2000#sch-1-sec-6"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-at-sea-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-at-sea-act-2000.pdf, p.25",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A charge of a maritime offence must not be brought in a court\ncontrary to the intergovernmental agreement.\n\n(2) If a charge of a maritime offence is brought in a court in\ncontravention of subclause (1), the court must, on application by\nthe Commonwealth Attorney-General or a participating State\nMinister, permanently stay the proceedings in that court.\n\n(3) However:\n\n(a) a contravention of subclause (1) does not affect a court’s\njurisdiction; and\n\n(b) if a charge of a maritime offence is brought in a court, the\ncourt will not (except on an application under subclause (2))\nbe concerned to enquire into whether the intergovernmental\nagreement has been complied with.\n\nSchedule 1  The cooperative scheme",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A charge of a maritime offence must not be brought in a court\ncontrary to the intergovernmental agreement.\n\n(2) If a charge of a maritime offence is brought in a court in\ncontravention of subclause (1), the court must, on application by\nthe Commonwealth Attorney-General or a participating State\nMinister, permanently stay the proceedings in that court.\n\n(3) However:\n\n(a) a contravention of subclause (1) does not affect a court’s\njurisdiction; and\n\n(b) if a charge of a maritime offence is brought in a court, the\ncourt will not (except on an application under subclause (2))\nbe concerned to enquire into whether the intergovernmental\nagreement has been complied with.\n\nSchedule 1  The cooperative scheme",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-at-sea-act-2000-sch-1-sec-6-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-at-sea-act-2000-sch-1-sec-6-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-at-sea-act-2000-sch-1-sec-6-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8d28dc7277292abc3e40e134dd9522d83cd8b09a77274adf968e3dc02d1c91de"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-at-sea-act-2000#sch-1-sec-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "6 Effect of the agreement",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 25,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A charge of a maritime offence must not be brought in a court\ncontrary to the intergovernmental agreement.\n\n(2) If a charge of a maritime offence is brought in a court in\ncontravention of subclause (1), the court must, on application by\nthe Commonwealth Attorney-General or a participating State\nMinister, permanently stay the proceedings in that court.\n\n(3) However:\n\n(a) a contravention of subclause (1) does not affect a court’s\njurisdiction; and\n\n(b) if a charge of a maritime offence is brought in a court, the\ncourt will not (except on an application under subclause (2))\nbe concerned to enquire into whether the intergovernmental\nagreement has been complied with.\n\nSchedule 1  The cooperative scheme"
    },
