      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-at-sea-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-at-sea-act-2000.pdf, p.28",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Governor-General may make regulations prescribing matters:\n\n(a) required or permitted by this scheme to be prescribed; or\n\n(b) necessary or convenient to be prescribed for carrying out or\ngiving effect to this scheme.\n\n(2) However, a regulation affecting the operation of this scheme in\nrelation to the inner adjacent area for a State may only be made\nwith the agreement of the participating State Minister for the\nrelevant State.\n\nThe cooperative scheme  Schedule 1\nAdjacent areas  Part 6\n\nClause 13\n\nCrimes at Sea Act 2000\nCompilation date: 30/8/19\nRegistered: 2/9/19",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Governor-General may make regulations prescribing matters:\n\n(a) required or permitted by this scheme to be prescribed; or\n\n(b) necessary or convenient to be prescribed for carrying out or\ngiving effect to this scheme.\n\n(2) However, a regulation affecting the operation of this scheme in\nrelation to the inner adjacent area for a State may only be made\nwith the agreement of the participating State Minister for the\nrelevant State.\n\nThe cooperative scheme  Schedule 1\nAdjacent areas  Part 6\n\nClause 13\n\nCrimes at Sea Act 2000\nCompilation date: 30/8/19\nRegistered: 2/9/19",
